{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The image confirms 字源’s main point about the historical 車 shapes and their reduction, but an embedded rare graph in its quotation has an uncertain Unicode identity. The broader claim is still legible, and I’m keeping that glyph unidentified rather than normalizing it. The same scanned page also includes the 車→车 forms, so I’m treating that as evidence for the graphic correspondence, not as proof of when modern 车 became standard."}}
