{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"李學勤主編《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012\",\"field\":\"車部 entry; PDF p.1260, printed p.1245; scan /home/catalin/hanzi-etymology-books/research-ocr/ziyuan-full/page-1260/source.png; inspected original pixels, including the 車 headword, historical-form rows, and paragraph\",\"text\":\"The entry is headed 車(车), gives the readings chē and a traditional phonological classification, and labels 車 a 形聲字. It quotes 說文’s account of 車 as the collective name for vehicle body and wheels and as pictographic, then discusses changing depictions: some oracle-bone and late Shang/early Zhou bronze forms omit features, and a reduced form is analyzed as a wheel-and-axle depiction. Its forms row includes oracle-bone, bronze, 說文 small-seal, regular 車, and regular 车. The book’s account is a distinct, more detailed analysis than a simple uniformly pictographic description; retain attribution and the book’s stated uncertainty around individual forms.\",\"record_character\":\"車\",\"kind\":\"local_book_scan\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\"title\":\"字源 (2012 edition; inspected PDF page 1260, printed page 1245)\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-04\"},{\"source\":\"Academia Sinica, Chinese Characters Database\",\"field\":\"車 graphic history\",\"text\":\"The database describes oracle forms of 車 as variable depictions of vehicle features, including wheels, body/framework, crossbar and yoke; later forms select features and develop toward regular 車. This supports a pictographic graphic history, though the book’s more specific account of a reduced form as wheel-and-axle is not independently established by this summary.\",\"record_character\":\"車\",\"kind\":\"external_dictionary\",\"url\":\"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=23348\",\"title\":\"漢字「車」：字形演變\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-04\"},{\"source\":\"Chinese University of Hong Kong, Multi-function Chinese Character Database\",\"field\":\"oracle-bone and bronze uses; graphic description\",\"text\":\"The database describes variable oracle and bronze forms that may show wheels, body, axle, yoke, pole and crossbar. It identifies oracle-bone examples Heji 11452 for vehicles (“six vehicles”), Heji 11450 for 車馬, and Heji 584 as a place-name use; bronze examples include vehicle and war-chariot uses. These are the database’s readings of cited inscriptions; it does not give calendar dates for those individual examples.\",\"record_character\":\"車\",\"kind\":\"primary_evidence_report\",\"url\":\"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E8%BB%8A&sub=1\",\"title\":\"漢語多功能字庫 — 車\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-04\"},{\"source\":\"Taiwan Ministry of Education, Concised Mandarin Chinese Dictionary\",\"field\":\"車 current Mandarin reading and senses\",\"text\":\"The inspected entry gives chē and lists vehicle, machinery using rotating axles, machine sewing/cutting, and a cartload measure without marking these senses obsolete or restricting them to historical quotations. This supports current lexicographic status for these senses, but does not date their semantic development.\",\"record_character\":\"車\",\"kind\":\"current_dictionary\",\"url\":\"https://dict.concised.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?ID=31626&la=1&powerMode=0\",\"title\":\"《國語辭典簡編本》：車\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-04\"},{\"source\":\"Unicode Consortium, Unihan Database\",\"field\":\"車 readings and simplified variant\",\"text\":\"The official Unihan record for U+8ECA lists kMandarin chē, kHanyuPinyin chē,jū, and simplified variant 车. This is current character metadata, not evidence for an ancient sound relationship or a historical explanation of simplification.\",\"record_character\":\"車\",\"kind\":\"official_character_metadata\",\"url\":\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=8ECA\",\"title\":\"Unihan data for U+8ECA\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-04\"},{\"source\":\"Local HSK1 Unihan extract\",\"field\":\"pipeline/data/unihan-kmandarin-hsk1.tsv; exact local row for 车\",\"text\":\"The supplied local row lists kMandarin for 车 as chē. This corroborates the current reading only; it does not establish historical sound relationships. The official Unihan record for the traditional counterpart is cited separately.\",\"record_character\":\"车\",\"kind\":\"local_reading_row\",\"url\":\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=8F66\",\"title\":\"Unihan data for U+8F66\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-04\"},{\"source\":\"国务院《汉字简化方案》, transcribed at Wikisource\",\"field\":\"1956 resolution and first simplified-character table\",\"text\":\"The resolution states the first table of 230 simplified characters was to be used in printed and handwritten documents from 1 February 1956. This supports the standardization date, not the origin of the earlier cursive form. The official Ministry page was located in search but opening it failed with a redirect loop; the inspected text here is the Wikisource transcription.\",\"record_character\":\"车\",\"kind\":\"primary_document_transcription\",\"url\":\"https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/%E6%BC%A2%E5%AD%97%E7%B0%A1%E5%8C%96%E6%96%B9%E6%A1%88\",\"title\":\"汉字简化方案 — 国务院关于公布汉字简化方案的决议\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-04\"}],\"search_audit\":[{\"query\":\"車 字源 甲骨文 車 字形演變 Academia Sinica; 车 繁简字 草书隋代 1956 简化字 車 字源; Chinese 車 oracle bone earliest vehicle use character dictionary; Taiwan MOE 車 dictionary chē vehicle current meaning\",\"urls\":[\"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=23348\",\"https://dict.concised.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?ID=31626&la=1&powerMode=0\",\"https://mdw.bnu.edu.cn/xsjl/xwgg/d77a2deba32b49d49b9a446b634844ad.htm\",\"https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/%E6%BC%A2%E5%AD%97%E7%B0%A1%E5%8C%96%E6%96%B9%E6%A1%88\",\"https://www.moe.gov.cn/jyb_xwfb/xw_fbh/moe_2128/moe_2326/moe_1144/tnull_14350.html\"],\"outcome\":\"Opened Academia Sinica, Taiwan MOE dictionary, BNU page, and Wikisource transcription. The BNU URL resolved to an unrelated essay and did not substantiate cursive 車 chronology. The MOE official resolution page appeared in search but opening failed with redirect loop.\"},{\"query\":\"site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl codepoint 8ECA Unihan; 车 简化字 来自 草书 Sui dynasty scholarly source 1956 scheme official; 車 Shang oracle bone use Heji 11452 six vehicles database\",\"urls\":[\"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E8%BB%8A&sub=1\",\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=8ECA\",\"https://www.moe.gov.cn/jyb_xwfb/xw_fbh/moe_2128/moe_2326/moe_1144/tnull_14350.html\"],\"outcome\":\"Inspected CUHK database and official Unihan page. The MOE URL again failed on open; no separate authoritative source establishing Sui-or-earlier cursive-form chronology was verified during this pass.\"}],\"gaps\":[\"[SCAN VERIFICATION REQUIRED] 字源 PDF p.1260, printed p.1245, quoted occurrence beginning 郭沫若《卜辞通纂》：“二车字一作…”. The book scan visibly contains embedded rare glyph drawings in this quotation; their exact scalar identities cannot be established from the typography/OCR. The quotation’s surrounding discussion is legible, but do not replace the drawings with guessed Unicode.\",\"The book’s claims about reduced forms and the particular wheel-and-axle interpretation are the author’s analysis; the inspected external summaries support variable pictorial forms and reduction but do not independently settle the identification of every reduced historical shape.\",\"The contemporary MOE entry inspected was Traditional Chinese 車. A verified official Unicode entry supplies 车’s kMandarin reading but not its current dictionary sense; current simplified-form sense documentation was not separately opened.\",\"The BNU URL cited in the supplied dossier resolves to an unrelated essay in this inspection, so no Sui-or-earlier date for cursive 车 is independently verified here. The 1956 standardization claim is supported only by the inspected transcription after the official Ministry page failed to open.\"]}"}}
